   "DATA LABELING",
   "03",
   "What is Polygon Annotation?",
   "Polygon annotation is a method of marking an object by clicking to create points around its edges. By connecting these points, you create a shape that closely follows the real shape and edges of the object.\nUnlike a rectangle, polygon annotation allows you to change direction and create different angles, making it useful for objects with irregular or complex shapes."
  ],
  "notes": "",
  "img": "assets/day2/polygon/s02.jpg"
 },
